      "output_tokens": 363,
      "patch_payload": {
        "candidate_id": "C_2122fe6391542480_1",
        "edit": "Swap the enable polarity: when ena is high, decode a into the one-hot output; when ena is low, force y to 0. This matches the oracle where cycle0 (ena=1, a=000) expects 00000000? No—observed expected at cycle0 is 00000000 while actual is 00000001, and cycle1 expected 00000001 while actual 00000000, indicating the enable condition was inverted. Moving the case into the ena-true branch and assigning y=0 in the else branch corrects the inverted enable behavior.",
        "lens_id": "dataflow_v1",
        "replacement_rtl": "\n\nmodule decoder3e_test(a,ena,y);\n  input [2:0] a;\n  input ena;\n  output reg [7:0] y; \n\n  \n\n\nalways @(*)begin\n  if(ena) begin\n    case(a)\n        3'b000: y = 8'b0000_0001;\n        3'b001: y = 8'b0000_0010;\n        3'b010: y = 8'b0000_0100;\n        3'b011: y = 8'b0000_1000;\n        3'b100: y = 8'b0001_0000;\n        3'b101: y = 8'b0010_0000;\n        3'b110: y = 8'b0100_0000;\n        3'b111: y = 8'b1000_0000;\n    \n    endcase\n  end\n  else y = 0;\nend\n\n\n\n\n\nendmodule\n",
        "slot_index": 1
      },
      "patch_payload_hash": "sha256:2cdbd61757be09df7fb215d96633aa6806fd5d8ac35c29f9d2944646c9ef27f8",
